{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
  "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Abood should be overruled because it failed to apply heightened First Amendment scrutiny to a compulsory fee for speech to influence governmental policies. Abood's failure places it at odds with Harris, with Knox, and a slew of other speech and association precedents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe that in the federal government generally, about a quarter of the workplace, a quarter to a third of the workplace is unionized."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So my other point was on the motion to dismiss issue, the need for a record, this case came up on a motion to dismiss. So I think the appropriate course is, as in Harris, you reverse the motion to dismiss and you send it back."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But even if there were some reliance, I think it would be very short-lived, until the next negotiating session, where any new decisions from this Court would be factored in."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's also what the United States argued in its Beck amicus brief here a few -- a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that the government's position as well, that all of that speech is a matter of public concern?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David L. Franklin",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court's cases uniformly recognize that the state has a much freer hand when it manages its personnel as an employer than when it regulates its citizens as a sovereign, and this has come up already today, that freer hand includes broad authority to put conditions on employees' speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David L. Franklin",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's one step removed from compelled speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, what is there -- what is there about compelled speech? I mean, our line has drawn a big difference between compelled speech and compelled subsidy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: It can be a partner with you in advocating for a greater size workforce, against privatization, against merit promotion, against -- for teacher tenure, for higher wages, for massive government, for increasing bonded indebtedness, for increasing taxes? That's -- that's the interest the state has?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Franklin",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FRANKLIN: I'm happy to speak to that, Justice Kagan. Here's what we know, and, obviously, we're on a motion to dismiss, but more broadly, what we know is that tangibly, when these kinds of obligations of financial support become voluntary, union membership goes down, union density rates go down, union resources go down. We've seen it again and again. Mancur Olson spoke about it in the foundational text of behavioral economics."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I'm asking you whether or not in your view, if you do not prevail in this case, the unions will have less political influence; yes or no?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: I think Abood used the word germaneness. But what Lehnert did was to give content to that because what Abood simply said was it is constitutional for this to happen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Didn't Abood draw -\u00ad talk about germaneness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Messenger",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "effectively a form of protection money, the idea that the government needs to force its employees to subsidize unions or otherwise the unions will disrupt the government, and I submit that's not an interest that this Court can accept as a compelling one for infringing on individuals' First Amendment rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1466",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "73db12a91b701e312e693efaa9e7d43783bdf6eef4c8f8a7a618cddc5b80b00e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73db12a91b70-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- Breyer said, every single decision affects the public fisc."
    },
